Z||000000||Spyro86SE||10-17-2000||05:56 PM||||i have this problem with my oil pressure that when i start the car in the morn it stays in the middle of the gauge but after awhile it drops to zero when i stop at a stop light or just stop it drops to zero but when i drive it stays in the middle of the gauge what could my problem be also would this effect my car to run hot any help would be very appreciated <P>thanks a bunch <BR>mikey ||||reg||1
Z||000001||sdm1964||10-17-2000||07:16 PM||||sounds like tome that you have an oil pump going or very worn bearings. Try switching to 20-50, slower cranking in the cold.||||reg||1
Z||000002||My7Fieros||10-17-2000||07:27 PM||||Yeah use heavier weight oil..works for me.<BR>And please start using punctuation.||||reg||1
Z||000003||hugh||10-17-2000||07:35 PM||||Before you do anything,you should use a known good gauge and sending unit and make sure your present gauge and sending unit are accurate.If they are,it would appear you have excessive wear in your engine,or an oil pump that is not up to snuff.If your engine is worn enough to cause the problem then you have nothing to lose by using heavier oil.But if you have no engine wear problems you should stick to factory recommendations.When you use oil that is too heavy you accelerate engine wear on cold startup(it takes too long for the oil to reach critical areas)If your car runs hot it will cause the oil pressure to be lower than normal(oil viscosity drops as the temperature rises)||||reg||1
